From: mayor <git@hough.ink>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 18:00:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 67/69] feat(scheduler): explain dispatch holds in gt scheduler
 status
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A freshly-scheduled ready bead with idle capacity sits undispatched until
the next daemon heartbeat (recovery_heartbeat_interval, default 3m) and can
be further deferred by pressure gating. With no signal for this, operators
(and the mayor) misread normal cadence as a head-of-line 'wedge' and reach
for gt scheduler clear.

Add a Dispatch: line (and dispatch_status JSON field) to gt scheduler status
that states why ready work is or isn't dispatching now: paused, no capacity,
direct-dispatch mode, or 'N ready — dispatches on next daemon heartbeat
(every 3m)'. The pressure caveat is shown only when pressure gating is
actually configured (thresholds default to 0/disabled).

Pure presentation logic derived from data the command already loads plus
operational config; no change to dispatch behavior. Covered by
scheduler_dispatch_status_test.go.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
